  "notes": [
    "This is a full, self-contained calendar-year 2026 cycle (January 4 through December 27), one entry per week.",
    "Most weeks list two or three prayer subjects side by side in the source's own table row; all are preserved as separate subjects in the order printed. A subject with no clergy/leader name in the source's own adjoining column has no `note` field, rather than a fabricated one.",
    "Several subjects are the source's own monthly heritage-month or awareness-observance texts (e.g. 'During Black History Month: In thanksgiving for...') rather than a parish or named ministry; these are recorded as `category` subjects using the source's full sentence as the name, since this corpus has no separate field for an observance.",
    "'Holy Host, Omaha' (June 21) and 'St. Peter's in the Valley, Lexington' (August 30, the Nebraska town, not the Kentucky diocese also in this corpus) are preserved exactly as printed.",
    "Several subjects naming a specific diocesan office-holder or observance by sentence (e.g. 'The retired Bishop of our Diocese: James E. Krotz', 'Our Diocesan Archivist: Jo Behrens, and all ministries which celebrate and remember the history of the Church') are recorded as `category` subjects using the full sentence as printed, since they are not a parish, and splitting out just the person's name would lose the source's own framing."
